SUMMARY:Free event/Jane's Walk. Toronto Islands Sunset Stroll. Dog friendl
 y
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n**RSVPs
  not needed for this one. Just show up and enjoy!**\n\nNOTE - it often fas
 ter to [buy your ferry ticket online in advance](https://secure.toronto.ca
 /FerryTicketOnline/tickets2/index.jsp)\n\nPart of the Jane's Walk [weekend
  of free walks. ](https://www.janeswalkfestivalto.com/walks)This one is le
 d by me.\n\nEnd your week with some surf\, sand\, and fun.\n\nA yearly Jan
 e's Walk tradition for me now\, I love to show off this magical place to b
 oth longtime visitors and people discovering them for the first time too. 
 The Toronto Islands are one of my favourite spots in all of the city for a
  multitude of reasons.\n\nLong to learn more about the rich history of the
  Toronto Islands? Participants will spot some amazing houses\, creep by a 
 haunted lighthouse\, walk on a rainbow\, see a giant hedge maze\, and more
 .\n\nThis is a dog friendly walk . So leashed\, well-behaved dogs are welc
 ome.\n\nWe will take the 6:45PM ferry to Hanlan's Point. All participants 
 are responsible for their ferry fares. We will walk from Hanlan's Point to
  Ward's Island with some brief stops along the way.\n\nWe will return on t
 he 9:45PM ferry from Ward's Island.\n\nWhile paths are all lit\, participa
 nts may want to bring headlights/flashlights for improved visibility.\n\nU
 pon arrival\, pay your ferry fare and then look for me in the waiting area
 . I'll be holding a Jane's Walk sign. I may even borrow a dog or two for t
 his adventure.
